## Summary

Part of #63 (Hunter). OpenRune had no implings: no catching, no impling jar loot and no crystal implings.

Depends: `content/hunter-module` (the Hunter module skeleton PR; this branch carries that commit and goes in after it merges, rebased then).

- Catching implings in Puro-Puro and Gielinor with a wielded butterfly net (or 10 extra Hunter levels barehanded) and an impling jar: 12% at level 1 to 98% at 99, +8 points barehanded or with a magic net.
- Impling data is a server-only dbtable `impling_types` (56002, rows 60152-60162) in the hunter pack: npc, Puro-Puro npc, jar, level, Puro-Puro and Gielinor XP, respawn ticks; own `ImplingPluginPack`. The ids are assigned by `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py` above the OSRS maximum per table, names prefixed `impling_`.
- Looting a caught impling jar rolls the jar's loot table; the empty jar comes back except for a 10% break chance. Dragon javelin tips only drop after Monkey Madness II (checked through `QuestRequirements`, as upstream does for other quest-gated content); without it the roll is over the rest of the dragon table. A tertiary clue scroll is not given while a clue or challenge scroll of that tier is in the inventory or bank, with the "You have a sneaking suspicion that you would have received a/an [tier] clue scroll." message.
- Crystal implings: one per world in Prifddinas, at one of 12 spots as one of the 17 named implings, a new one 3 minutes after each :00 and :30 (UTC) and one at server start; Hunter 80 (90 barehanded), 280 XP. Their catch chance is their own curve: the OSRS skilling formula with low 8 / high 141 with a butterfly net (116/256 at 80 to 142/256 at 99) and 28 / 161 barehanded or with a magic net (+20/256, the wiki's 7.8%).

