## How it was tested

- `ImplingScriptTest` (new, `content:skills:hunter` integration, 4 tests): the catch chance runs from 12 to 98 percent, plus 8 with a magic net; a catch swaps one jar for the impling jar and gives Hunter XP; no jar, nothing moves; barehanded needs ten more levels.
- `ImplingLootScriptTest` (new, 7 tests): every caught jar has a loot table whose main table sums to one; Loot is the jars' third inventory op, which the client sends as op 3; the first main-table line comes out when every roll is zero; dragon javelin tips only drop after Monkey Madness II; a held tier's clue scroll is skipped; a clue scroll in the bank counts as held; looting swaps the jar for loot.
- `CrystalImplingScriptTest` (new, 3 tests): a new half hour starts three minutes past; the catch curve matches the wiki chart (all 40 points: net and bonus at each level 80-99); one crystal impling at a time, on a wiki spot.
- Fork CI (GitHub Actions: freshCache, buildCache, assemble test integration, boot) green at the commit.
- Not checked in game on this commit (the integration tests cover the flow); the upstream gate's in-game re-check is still to come.

## Checklist

- [x] Builds and the server boots
- [x] Tests only cover complex logic and anything that moves items (no dupes): the catch curves, the loot roll rules, and the jar swaps on catch and loot
- [ ] Gamevals symbols instead of raw ids; game data in the cache, not Kotlin maps: impling data is in the server-only dbtable; the jar loot tables are a Kotlin table generated from the wiki's jar pages (`ImplingLootTables.kt`, OSRS obj ids), not cache data
- [x] State in varbits/varps, not attrs: no player state; the crystal impling is one server-wide npc
- [ ] Matches the OSRS wiki (deviations noted in `docs/quirks.md`): the deviations are listed under Caveats below, not in `docs/quirks.md`
- [ ] New content checked against rsprox dumps where possible (anims, projectiles, sounds, timings): no recording of an impling catch (only impling-jar crafting at the Chemist, recording 468, which this PR does not cover) exists among the 27 local RSProx transcripts, and rsprox.net's index has no topic search; the timings stay as the wiki and the caveats say
